### 5.5 Assessment

The site receives excellent solar irradiance with an annual GHI of {{ solar.annual_ghi_kwh_m2 | num(1) }} kWh/m², which is {% if solar.annual_ghi_kwh_m2 > 1800 %}well above{% elif solar.annual_ghi_kwh_m2 > 1500 %}above{% else %}within{% endif %} the typical range for economically viable solar mini-grids in Sub-Saharan Africa (1,500–2,200 kWh/m²/yr). Seasonal variation between the sunniest and dullest months is approximately {{ ((solar.monthly_ghi_kwh_m2 | max) / (solar.monthly_ghi_kwh_m2 | min) * 100 - 100) | num(0) }}%, which {% if ((solar.monthly_ghi_kwh_m2 | max) / (solar.monthly_ghi_kwh_m2 | min)) < 1.5 %}is moderate and manageable{% else %}is notable and influences battery sizing{% endif %}.

